is going to  create those tack points of that piece  of tissue  um that is not going to damage your  nucleic acid integrity on that  particular  part of your your tissue  all right thank you  uh  [Music]  next question  what are the different applications  people are using the arcturus for  um yes so that is a great question so  for lcm we really see a wide array of  different applications that it's used  for um obviously oncology is a huge  application because of all the reasons  that i expressed in this presentation  but in addition to oncology one of the  biggest fields that we see using our  technology is neuroscience  um it's a great candidate for lcm  because a lot of the same reasons as  oncology so that need for isolating out  pure populations when you're looking at  endothelial heterogeneity within that  nervous system  um other applications we see are  forensics and um human identification as  well as plant biology actually so um  really any research application where  you need to separate pure populations  would be a really great candidate for  using lcm  all right great thank you  um next question  does the arcturus select need the laser  spot optimized  yes and i i know it can be it can be a  little tedious at the beginning of your  capture um your capture session um but  really it's just to ensure that you know  the laser's firing in the right spot  that it's optimized for  you know your type of tissue the type of  cap you're using i'm just kind of making  sure that before you go to actually  capture your um your tissue that you  know you're going to fire in the spot  that you want it to be  um because you don't want to risk  wasting uh precious tissue especially if  you're looking at archival slides and  things like that where you don't have  the luxury  of a bunch of extra tissue to practice  on so  um that is i know it's tedious but um  you get the hang of it pretty fast  all right  uh next question what sort of customers  would benefit the most fro